 "sentences": [
  "This composer had a secret literary alter ego.",
  "Sir Arnold Bax was a famous English musician who wrote seven symphonies.",
  "Born into a wealthy family, he followed his own artistic path without worrying about trends.",
  "He even lived in Ireland, writing fiction and verse under the name Dermot O'Byrne.",
  "Later, he traded his early Celtic obsession for a deep fascination with Nordic culture.",
  "He remains an important but isolated figure in history."
